  "question": {
    "text": "Adsorption of a gas follows Freundlich adsorption isotherm. In the given plot, <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi></math> is the mass of the gas adsorbed on mass <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> of the adsorbent at pressure (P). if <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup></math> find the magnitude of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">‘</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">’</mi></math> is ------.<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0010_f38d863b5dab.png\" style=\"width: 165px; height: 135px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to Freundlich adsorption isotherm,<br /><math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />So, <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></math><br />Therefore, value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">'</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">'</mi></math> is <math><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math>"
  }
